    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7556" root="حرب" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَارِثٌ</span></b>  <i>A collector of property.</i> (Msb.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَارِثُ</span>, (K, [also written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحٰرِثُ</span>, in the CK,
erroneously, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الحَرَثُ</span>,]) as a generic proper name,
(MF,) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبُو الحَارِثِ</span>, (S, K,) the latter the
better known, (TA,) <i>The lion:</i> (S, K:) because
he is the prince of beasts of prey, and the strongest
to acquire. (Har p. 662.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَرَّاثٌ</span>.

